## 10. Summary Statement for Claude

This project is a research-grade systematic trading model, not a passive index tracker. The objective is durable, testable alpha, primarily through expanding into emerging markets, small caps, and overlooked names, while preserving backtest integrity, avoiding survivorship bias, and prioritising risk-adjusted performance over headline compound annual growth rate. Reference universe: MSCI Emerging Markets (~1,197 names, 24 countries), EEM, IEMG, SPEM, EMXC, FRDM, and example stocks such as Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing, Tencent, Alibaba, Samsung Electronics, HDFC Bank, and MercadoLibre. Core formulas: 12-month and 12-1 momentum, 52-week high ratio, volatility-adjusted momentum, inverse-volatility sizing, and the 45/25/30 composite score blend. [fool](https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/07/18/this-emerging-markets-etf-beat-sp-500-for-16-years/)